{"resourceIdentifier":"2746","resourceName":"Guangzhou Eastern Solid Resource Recycling Center MSW Integrated treatment Plant Project","description":"Guangzhou Eastern Solid Resource Recycling Center MSW Integrated treatment Plant Project (hereinafter referred to as the project) is located at the Solid Resource Recycling Center, Fushan Village, Jiulong Town, Luogang District, Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, P.R China.\r\nThe purpose of the project is to treat MSW with anaerobic digesters and utilize recovered biogas for electricity generation. The project activity includes MSW collection, MSW pre-treatment system, biodiesel production system, anaerobic digester, biogas purification, electricity generation system and waste heat recovery. \r\nThe fresh waste of the project is mainly kitchen and catering waste of the Guangzhou City and the design processing capacity of the project for the fresh waste is 2,040 tonnes per day. The biogas from anaerobic digestion will be used for electricity generation with internal combustion generators. The total installed capacity will be 10.34 MW included 4 generators with each 1.063 MW and 2 generators with each 3.044 MW. \r\nBefore the implementation of the project activity, the fresh waste would be treated in a landfill site with a partial capture of the landfill gas (LFG) and flaring of the captured LFG. The project is to utilize the biogas produced by anaerobic digestion for power generation. The electricity generated by the project is supplied to China South Power Grid (CSPG) which is dominated by coal-fired power stations. \r\nIn absence of the project, equivalent amount of electricity exported to the grid by the project would have otherwise been supplied by China South Power Grid (CSPG). Greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions will be reduced by avoiding CO2 emissions from those fossil fuel-based power plants connected to the grid and by avoiding GHG emissions from venting LFG into atmosphere at the landfill site.","location":{"latitude":23.284444,"longitude":113.515000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-12-21","endExclusive":"2022-01-21","endInclusive":"2022-01-20"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2746"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangdong"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangzhou LEO-KING Environmental Technology Co., Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"Guangdong Province, China"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2746"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"359014"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0022"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CTI Certification Co., Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"23/08/2022"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 01/04/2020 - 31/03/2027"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=58126&IDKEY=k8723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq0a80155754","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"01-Guangzhou_VCS-Joint-Project-Description-Monitoring-Report_V01.pdf","uploadDate":"2021-11-25T13:34:27.187Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=58128&IDKEY=ciofj09234rm9oq4jndsma80vcalksdjf98cxkjaf90823nmq3q80158512","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"03-Guangzhou_VCS Listing Representation.pdf","uploadDate":"2021-11-25T13:35:25.13Z